#: colorscm.cpp:252
msgid "Apply colors to &non-KDE applications"
msgstr "Klören ok för Programmen bruken, de nich deel vun KDE sünn."

#: colorscm.cpp:256
msgid "Check this box to apply the current color scheme to GTK applications."
msgstr ""

#: colorscm.cpp:413
msgid ""
"<h1>Colors</h1> This module allows you to choose the color scheme used for "
"the KDE desktop. The different elements of the desktop, such as title bars, "
"menu text, etc., are called \"widgets\". You can choose the widget whose "
"color you want to change by selecting it from a list, or by clicking on a "
"graphical representation of the desktop."
"<p>"
" You can save color settings as complete color schemes, which can also be "
"modified or deleted. KDE comes with several predefined color schemes on "
"which you can base your own."
"<p> All KDE applications will obey the selected color scheme. Non-KDE "
"applications may also obey some or all of the color settings. See the "
"\"Style\" control module for more details."
msgstr ""

#: colorscm.cpp:488
msgid ""
"This color scheme could not be removed.\n"
